    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s rotation today, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (75.25) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) lead the charge as our clear top-tier plays. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a, with a 10% boost from the SP\u2019s xERA, while **Jonathan Aranda** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance hitting second against Jobe, buoyed by a substantial 12% platoon advantage. **Lawrence Butler** (69.79) also warrants elite consideration; despite a modest base, his 13% platoon boost against Bradley creates a strong scoring environment. Meanwhile, **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.35) remains an intriguing start, as the combination of wind out and a favorable matchup against Singer maximizes his upside in our 5x5 Roto framework.\n\nThe tightest decision of the day centered on the bench, where **Gleyber Torres** (50.38) just narrowly missed the cut. While **Gleyber Torres** offered a strong +10% boost from his lead-off spot, the efficiency projections preferred the defensive and situational consistency of **Cal Raleigh** (50.78) and **Justin Crawford** (50.89). We continue to prioritize **Justin Crawford** despite his lower-order placement because of his elite sprint speed, which remains the primary engine for our category scarcity strategy. \n\nWe are monitoring several risks heading into first pitch. With lineups for **Luis Arraez**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Bryce Harper** still pending, any shift in the batting order could trigger a recalculation, particularly for **Justin Crawford** and **Luis Arraez**, who are sensitive to drops in lineup position. Additionally, while **Bryce Harper** (61.17) is projected as a strong start, his performance against Kirby will be heavily scrutinized given his high xwOBA. We remain mindful that **Will Smith** is currently sidelined on the IL, requiring us to rely on our active core to maintain our pace in Roto categories.",
